    "chunk_text": "This Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk1A - G 30945\u2014 27 (09/2019)\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'09'10PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 10.09.20192A\n\n(3) Each Tourist Guide Lecturer shall possess the minimum requirements and qualifications specified inSchedule I and Schedule II hereto as applicable.\n\nPART I\n\nRegistration & Licensing of Tourist Guide Lecturers\n\n3. Every person who desires to carry on a service of a tourist guide lecturer under these regulations shall -\n\n(a)submit applications for registration and licensing separately to the Director- General of the Sri LankaTourism Development Authority (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cDirector-General\u201d) in forms as may bedetermined by him ;\n\n(b)pay such fees specified in the Order made under subsection (5) of Section 48 of the Tourism Act, No.38 of 2005 and published in Extraordinary Gazette No. 2071/57 of May 16, 2018 together with theapplications.\n\n(c)submit a valid medical certificate issued by a registered government medical officer certifying theapplicant is mentally and physically fit to function as a tourist guide lecturer.\n\n(d)submit a valid proof of successful completion of training and skills development related to touristguiding amounting to a minimum of 32 hours per annum conducted by Sri Lanka Institute of Tourism andHotel Management, Sri Lanka Institute of National Tourist Guide lecturers or any other training instituteauthorized by the Authority ; and\n\n(e)submit a police certificate of non-conviction\n\n4. The Director General may request for further information or documents to be furnished, including anyclarification that he may consider to be necessary for the purpose of deciding such application.\n\n5. An application found to contain false, misleading or incorrect information or particulars shall be rejected."
