    "chunk_text": "(b)shall come into force on the date specified therein ; and\n\n(c)shall unless it is earlier cancelled or revoked by the Director-General, remain in force for a period ofone year from the date specified in the license.\n\nPART II\n\nGeneral Provisions\n\n11. The Director-General may on the approval of the Authority amend, modify or rescind any term or conditionattached to the license issued under regulation 8 of these regulations.\n\n12. The Director-General shall cancel the license issued under regulation 8 of these regulations on the ground -\n\n(a)that any provision of the Tourism Act, No. 38 of 2005 has been violated ;(b)that any regulation made under the Tourism Act, No. 38 of 2005 has been violated ; or(c)that any condition attached to the license issued under regulation 8 of these regulations has not beencomplied with.\n\n13. A license issued under regulation 8 of these regulations shall be renewable -\n\n(a)on an application being made in that behalf to the Director-General in a form as may be determined byhim ;(b)not less than 3 months before the expiry of the license ; and(c)upon payment of such fees as are payable in terms of the Order made under subsection (5) of section 48of the Tourism Act, No. 38 of 2005 and published in Gazette Extraordinary No. 2071/57 of May 16,2018.\n\n14. Any person aggrieved by a decision of a refusal or renewal or a cancellation of a license issued may, withinone month from the date of receipt of the written communication informing such person of the refusal or the cancellation,as the case may be submit an appeal to the tribunal established under Section 51 of the Tourism Act, No. 38 of 2005.\n\n15. The Director-General shall casue to maintain a Register of services of tourist guide lecturers which shallcontain such particulars of the registered and licensed tourist guide services and be maintained in such form as may bedetermined by the Director-General."
